; Sample LinuxCNC tool table for lcncgui documentation.
; Point [EMCIO] TOOL_TABLE in your INI to this file (or merge lines into your real table).
; After editing on disk, use the refresh control in the Tools screen or restart LinuxCNC.
;
; Format (typical mill): T<pocket> P<pocket> ... offsets ... D<diameter> ; optional short comment
; lcncgui library data (name, type, presets, …) lives in sample_tool_table.lcncgui-tools.json beside this file.

T1 P1 Z+0.000000 D+6.000000 ; VHM Schaftfräser 6mm
T2 P2 Z+0.000000 D+10.000000 ; VHM Schaftfräser 10mm
T3 P3 Z+0.000000 D+5.000000 ; HSS Spiralbohrer 5mm
T4 P4 Z+0.000000 D+1.000000 ; VHM Mikrofräser 1mm
T5 P5 Z+0.000000 D+10.000000 ; Kegelsenker 90° 10mm
